(ICA - Applying for Singapore Permanent Residence \(PR\)) '
() '
(AGENCY: Immigration & Checkpoints Authority \(ICA\)) '
(CATEGORY: Residency) '
(TOPIC: Apply for Permanent Residence) '
(SOURCE_URL: https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/PR/apply) '
(LAST_VERIFIED: 2026-10-28) '
() '
(Eligibility - you may be eligible if you are one of the following:) '
(- A spouse of a Singapore citizen or permanent resident \(PR\)) '
(- An unmarried child under 21 of a Singapore citizen or PR,) '
(  through a legal marriage or legal adoption) '
(- An aged parent of a Singapore citizen aged 21 or older) '
(- A holder of an Employment Pass or S Pass) '
(- A student in Singapore who has passed at least one national exam,) '
(  or is in the Integrated Programme \(IP\)) '
(- A foreign investor \(check the EDB website for the Global Investor) '
(  Programme\)) '
() '
(How to apply: through ICA e-Service. Applicants generally need Singpass.) '
(A spouse sponsor logs in to ICA e-Service with Singpass to sponsor the) '
(application. Students under 15 can use the non-Singpass option.) '
() '
(Fees \(non-refundable, paid online\):) '
(- S$100 per application, at submission) '
(- On completion of formalities: S$20 Entry Permit,) '
(  S$50 5-year Re-Entry Permit, S$50 Singapore Identity Card) '
() '
(Processing time: applications are processed within 6 months if all) '
(required documents are submitted and in order. Some may take longer.) '
() '
(Official source: https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/PR/apply) '
ET
endstream
